        <h1 class="post-detail__title">#WhyItMatters – Teton Valley Hospital Foundation</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/49311.webp" alt="#WhyItMatters – Teton Valley Hospital Foundation" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p><strong><em>Each year, local nonprofits come together to participate in the annual Tin Cup Challenge hosted by the Community Foundation of Teton Valley.  These nonprofits work tirelessly within our community to provide programs and services that improve lives in Teton Valley.  Serving as both a 9-week campaign for giving and a one-day event celebrating our community’s spirit of generosity, the annual fundraiser allows these local organizations to focus more fully on the work of their mission while providing them with an opportunity to raise and then leverage the funds needed to fulfill their mission.  </em></strong></p>
<p><strong>The Teton Valley Hospital Foundation is one such organization…</strong></p>
<p><em>Submitted by Teton Valley Health Care</em></p>
<p>If you were lucky enough to avoid the need for medical care last year, may your good fortune continue through 2016.  For the rest of us, there’s a good chance that people who contribute to Teton Valley Hospital Foundation had a hand in your care.</p>
<p>Last year, our ambulance was called out 517 times. It carries new equipment for heart attack and respiratory emergencies. Thank you, Teton Valley Hospital Foundation.</p>
<p>Our Emergency Room crew helped 1,691 people. The ER exam rooms have new monitors and medical instruments to enhance patient care. Thank you.</p>
<p>Specialists delivered 6,469 outpatient surgeries and services. Our OR suites offered a new adjustable surgical table, enhanced lighting fixtures and specialty instrumentation. Thank you.</p>
<p>Over 420 people received mammograms and were wrapped in warmed robes for their exam.  Over 30 people were given free mammograms. Thank you.</p>
<p>We delivered 2,421 X-rays using new, technologically advanced X-ray equipment in a completely renovated suite funded in part by our Foundation.  Thousands of thanks.</p>
<p>The Hospital Foundation has a crucial role in the sustainability of our community hospital. People who donate to Teton Valley Hospital Foundation care about matters of life and death; healing and wellness. The Tin Cup Challenge has helped fund specific healthcare needs for our friends, family and neighbors. You can help make sure everyone has access to the best medical care possible by choosing to invest in community healthcare.</p>
<p>Interested in a tour of Teton Valley Hospital? You may be pleasantly surprised by the advanced diagnostic and specialty capabilities of our rural hospital.  Call Ann at (208) 354-6301 or info@tvhcare.org to schedule.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
